{"schema":"literary-friend.reference-page.v1","originalPath":"assets/fontforge-reference/doc/sphinx/olddocs/old/ja/MetaFont.html","title":"MetaFont — フォントに対する標準的な変形","sourceSha256":"bb2a3401c8de33bbdb974f26e7f378f298dd4e8af30fa456473e9c9dc26f1d00","headingIndex":[{"level":1,"text":"MetaFont フォントに対する標準的変形"},{"level":3,"text":"ボールド"},{"level":3,"text":"ポイントサイズ"},{"level":3,"text":"スモールキャップ (小型大文字)"},{"level":3,"text":"イタリック"},{"level":3,"text":"オブリーク (傾斜体)"},{"level":3,"text":"エクステンディド/コンデンスト"},{"level":3,"text":""}],"scripts":[],"styles":[],"documentTree":[{"tag":"html","attributes":{},"children":["\n",{"tag":"head","attributes":{},"children":["\n",{"comment":" Created with AOLpress/2.0 "},"\n",{"comment":" AP: Created on: 23-Jun-2001 "},"\n",{"comment":" AP: Last modified: 13-Oct-2004 "},"\n",{"tag":"meta","attributes":{"http-equiv":"Content-Type","content":"text/html; charset=utf-8"},"children":[]},"\n",{"comment":"<TITLE>MetaFont - - Standard Transformations on Fonts</TITLE>"},"\n",{"tag":"title","attributes":{},"children":["MetaFont — フォントに対する標準的な変形"]},"\n",{"tag":"link","attributes":{"rel":"icon","href":"../../_static/fftype16.png"},"children":[]},"\n",{"tag":"link","attributes":{"rel":"stylesheet","type":"text/css","href":"FontForge.css"},"children":[]},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"body","attributes":{},"children":["\n",{"tag":"div","attributes":{"id":"in"},"children":["\n",{"tag":"h1","attributes":{"align":"Center"},"children":["\n  MetaFont",{"tag":"br","attributes":{},"children":[]},"\n",{"comment":"\n  Standard Transformations on Fonts "},"\n  フォントに対する標準的変形\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","attributes":{},"children":["\n",{"comment":"\nThe MetaFont dialog (obviously the name is a rip-off of\n<A HREF=\"http://www.tug.org/\">Knuth's work</A>) will try to find important\nfeatures of a font and a glyph and allow you to modify them. It does\n<EM>not</EM> read TeX .mf files. The features searched for are: "},"\nMetaFont ダイアログ (明らかにこの名前は ",{"tag":"a","attributes":{"href":"http://www.tug.org/"},"children":["Knuth の仕事"]},"からの借り物です) は、フォントの重要な特徴を検出し、それを変更できるようにしようと試みます。これは TeX の .mf ファイルを読み込み",{"tag":"em","attributes":{},"children":["ません"]},"。検索する機能は以下のとおりです:\n"]},{"tag":"ul","attributes":{},"children":["\n",{"tag":"li","attributes":{},"children":["\n",{"comment":"The X-Height.<BR>\n    A font-wide attribute, making the X-Height larger relative to the Cap-Height\n    will often make the font appear to have a larger point-size (FontForge will\n    also search out the Cap-Height, Ascender-Height and Descender, but modification\n    of those is less common. Though it is feasible) "},"\n    x ハイト",{"tag":"br","attributes":{},"children":[]},"\n    フォント全体に通底する属性で、x ハイトをキャップハイトに比べて相対的に大きくすると、多くの場合フォントが大きなポイントサイズをもっているように見えます (FontForge はキャップハイト、アセンダおよびディセンダも調べますが、これらを変更するのはあまり一般的ではありません。それは実現可能ではあるでしょうが)\n  "]},{"tag":"li","attributes":{},"children":["\n",{"comment":"Stems and their widths<BR>\n    Modification of a Stem's width makes the font appear Bolder or Lighter "},"\n    ステムとその幅",{"tag":"br","attributes":{},"children":[]},"\n    ステムの幅を変更すると、フォントがより太く、またはより細くなります。\n  "]},{"tag":"li","attributes":{},"children":["\n",{"comment":"Counters and their widths (a counter is the white space between stems)<BR>\n    Modification of a Counter's width makes the font appear Expanded or Condensed "},"\n    カウンタとその幅 (カウンタとは、ステム間のホワイトスペースです)",{"tag":"br","attributes":{},"children":[]},"\n    カウンタの幅を変更すると、フォントがエキスパンデドまたはコンデンストに変わります。\n  "]},{"tag":"li","attributes":{},"children":["\n",{"comment":"Left and Right Side Bearings<BR>\n    Behavior similar to Counter's "},"\n    左右のサイドベアリング",{"tag":"br","attributes":{},"children":[]},"\n    カウンタと同様にふるまいます。\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"p","attributes":{},"children":["\n",{"comment":"\nThe results will probably always need to be examined and fixed up by the\nhuman eye, but they may provide a help in changing a font's attributes. At\nthe moment the command is pretty primitive. "},"\nおそらく、結果は常に人間の目で確認してから修正を施す必要があるでしょう。とは言え、これらはフォントの属性を変更するのに助けとなるでしょう。現時点では、このコマンドは非常に原始的です。\n"]},{"tag":"p","attributes":{},"children":["\n",{"comment":"\nIt \"works\" best on sans serif, non-Oblique fonts.  "},"\nこれはサンセリフの、傾いていないフォントにおいて最もうまく“働き”ます。\n  "]},{"tag":"hr","attributes":{},"children":[]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","attributes":{},"children":["\n",{"comment":"Bold"},"\n    ボールド\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","attributes":{},"children":["\n",{"comment":"\nBold fonts have thicker stems and are slightly more extended than normal\nfonts. In Knuth's Computers &amp; Typesetting, the bold fonts have a stem\nwidth that is approximately 1.6 (1.68(at 12pt)-1.5(at 5pt)) times the stem\nwidth of the normal font. This is very similar to the 1.75 suggested by\nMicrosoft's ratio of 700/400 (700 being the numeric weight of a bold font,\nand 400 being the numeric weight of a normal font). "},"\nボールドフォントはノーマルフォントよりも太いステムをもち、わずかに幅が広げられています。Knuth の Computers & Typesetting では、ボールドフォントはノーマルフォントの約1.6倍 (1.68倍(12pt)〜1.5倍(5pt)) のステム幅をもっています。これは、Microsoft による 700/400 (700 はボールドフォントのウェイトを表す数値で、400 はノーマルフォントのウェイトを表す数値です) という比率が示唆する 1.75 という値とほぼ同じです。\n"]},{"tag":"p","attributes":{},"children":["\n",{"comment":"\nIn Knuth's Computer Modern Bold Extended Roman, the \"m\" glyph is extended\nto 1.15 times the width of the \"m\" in Computer Modern Roman, and the x-height\nis 1.03 times higher. "},"\nKnuth の Computer Modern Bold Extended Roman では、“m”のグリフは Computer Modern Roman の“m”の 1.15 倍に広げられており、x ハイトは 1.03 倍高くなっています。\n"]},{"tag":"p","attributes":{},"children":["\n"]},{"tag":"table","attributes":{"border":"","cellpadding":"2"},"children":["\n",{"tag":"tr","attributes":{},"children":["\n",{"comment":"<TD>Font</TD>"},"\n",{"tag":"td","attributes":{},"children":["フォント"]},"\n",{"comment":"<TD>Ratio of Bold/Regular Stems</TD>"},"\n",{"tag":"td","attributes":{},"children":["Bold/Regular のステムの比率"]},"\n",{"comment":"<TD>Ratio of DemiBold/Regular</TD> "},"\n",{"tag":"td","attributes":{},"children":["DemiBold/Regular の比率"]},"\n",{"comment":"<TD>Expansion</TD> "},"\n",{"tag":"td","attributes":{},"children":["幅の拡大率"]},"\n",{"comment":"<TD>Bold serif height/Regular serif</TD> "},"\n",{"tag":"td","attributes":{},"children":["Bold のセリフ高/Regular のセリフ高"]},"\n",{"comment":"<TD>Bold serif width/regular</TD> "},"\n",{"tag":"td","attributes":{},"children":["Bold のセリフ幅/Regular"]},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","attributes":{},"children":["\n",{"tag":"td","attributes":{},"children":["Arial"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","attributes":{},"children":["1.5"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","attributes":{},"children":[]},"\n",{"tag":"td","attributes":{},"children":["1"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","attributes":{},"children":[]},"\n",{"tag":"td","attributes":{},"children":[]},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","attributes":{},"children":["\n",{"tag":"td","attributes":{},"children":["Times New Roman"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","attributes":{},"children":["1.7"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","attributes":{},"children":[]},"\n",{"tag":"td","attributes":{},"children":[]},"\n",{"tag":"td","attributes":{},"children":["1"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","attributes":{},"children":[".98"]},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","attributes":{},"children":["\n",{"tag":"td","attributes":{},"children":["Computer Modern Roman"]},"\n",{"comment":"<TD>1.68(at 12pt) - 1.5(at 5pt)</TD>"},"\n",{"tag":"td","attributes":{},"children":["1.68(12ptの時)〜1.5(5ptの時)"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","attributes":{},"children":[]},"\n",{"tag":"td","attributes":{},"children":["1.15"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","attributes":{},"children":[]},"\n",{"tag":"td","attributes":{},"children":[]},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","attributes":{},"children":["\n",{"tag":"td","attributes":{},"children":["Adobe Helvetica"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","attributes":{},"children":["1.6"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","attributes":{},"children":[]},"\n",{"tag":"td","attributes":{},"children":[]},"\n",{"tag":"td","attributes":{},"children":[]},"\n",{"tag":"td","attributes":{},"children":[]},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","attributes":{},"children":["\n",{"tag":"td","attributes":{},"children":["Adobe Times"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","attributes":{},"children":["1.56"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","attributes":{},"children":[]},"\n",{"tag":"td","attributes":{},"children":["1.17"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","attributes":{},"children":["1.10"]},"\n",{"comment":"<TD>.97</TD>"},"\n",{"tag":"td","attributes":{},"children":["0.97"]},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","attributes":{},"children":["\n",{"tag":"td","attributes":{},"children":["Garamond Antiqua"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","attributes":{},"children":[]},"\n",{"tag":"td","attributes":{},"children":["1.5"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","attributes":{},"children":[]},"\n",{"tag":"td","attributes":{},"children":["1.05"]},"\n",{"comment":"<TD>.90</TD>"},"\n",{"tag":"td","attributes":{},"children":["0.90"]},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","attributes":{},"children":["\n",{"tag":"td","attributes":{},"children":[]},"\n",{"tag":"td","attributes":{},"children":[]},"\n",{"tag":"td","attributes":{},"children":[]},"\n",{"tag":"td","attributes":{},"children":[]},"\n",{"tag":"td","attributes":{},"children":[]},"\n",{"tag":"td","attributes":{},"children":[]},"\n"]},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","attributes":{},"children":["\n"]},{"tag":"h3","attributes":{},"children":["\n",{"comment":"Point Size"},"\n    ポイントサイズ\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","attributes":{},"children":["\n",{"comment":"\nAt first glance this does not seem like much of a transformation, after all\npostscript and truetype fonts can be drawn at any pointsize. But traditionally,\nas the point-size decreases the boldness (thickness of the stems) increases\nslightly, the counters and side bearings also change. For metal type there\nwere generally three drawings for a glyph in a given font, one for pointsizes\nless than 10, one for pointsizes 10,11 and 12, and one for display sizes\n(above 12). Most computer vector fonts do not show this change, while Knuth's\nComputer Modern fonts have a continuum: "},"\nPostScript にしろ TrueType にしろ任意のポイントサイズで描けるわけですから、一見して、これは他の変形とはまったく別問題のように見えます。しかし伝統的には、ポイントサイズが小さくなるにつれてボールドネス (ステムの太さ) をわずかに増やし、カウンタとサイドベアリングもそれに合わせて変化させていました。金属活字では一般に、フォント 1 つに対して 3 個の原字が用いられていました。1 個は 10 ポイント未満のサイズ用、1 個は 10, 11 および 12 ポイント用、もう 1 個は (12 ポイントを超える) ディスプレイサイズ用でした。ほとんどの計算機用ベクトルフォントはこの変化を見せませんが、Knuth の Computer Modern フォントは以下のように連続的に変化します:\n"]},{"tag":"table","attributes":{"cellpadding":"2"},"children":["\n",{"tag":"caption","attributes":{},"children":["\n",{"comment":"Stem width, scaled by point size, made relative to 12pt"},"\n    ステム幅、ポイントサイズで縮小して、12 ポイントと相対的に比較した値\n  "]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","attributes":{},"children":["\n",{"tag":"td","attributes":{},"children":[]},"\n",{"tag":"th","attributes":{},"children":["17pt"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","attributes":{},"children":["12pt"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","attributes":{},"children":["10pt"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","attributes":{},"children":["9pt"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","attributes":{},"children":["8pt"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","attributes":{},"children":["7pt"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","attributes":{},"children":["6pt"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","attributes":{},"children":["5pt"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","attributes":{},"children":[]},"\n",{"comment":"<TH>(12pt compared to cmr 12pt)</TH>"},"\n",{"tag":"th","attributes":{},"children":["(cmr 12pt に対する 12pt 時の値)"]},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","attributes":{},"children":["\n",{"tag":"th","attributes":{},"children":["cmr"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","attributes":{},"children":["83%"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","attributes":{},"children":["100%"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","attributes":{},"children":["109%"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","attributes":{},"children":["116%"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","attributes":{},"children":["120%"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","attributes":{},"children":["124%"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","attributes":{},"children":["130%"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","attributes":{},"children":["139%"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","attributes":{},"children":["Computer Modern Roman"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","attributes":{},"children":["100%"]},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","attributes":{},"children":["\n",{"tag":"th","attributes":{},"children":["cmti"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","attributes":{},"children":[]},"\n",{"tag":"td","attributes":{},"children":["100%"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","attributes":